          "heading": "Expert FAQ Stack",
          "faqs": [
            {
              "q": "What are the primary operational challenges during commercial electric vehicle adoption?",
              "a": "Fleet directors typically prioritize three major variables: high initial vehicle capital costs, the extensive capital needed to install industrial charging hardware, and range reliability under variable cargo weights or extreme winter conditions."
            },
            {
              "q": "How does Hudson County Motors assist with depot charging layout planning?",
              "a": "When a fleet acquires an electric truck asset, our specialists perform site design audits and consult with local utilities to establish the necessary charging logistics, helping to avoid expensive power-up delays."
            },
            {
              "q": "Which industrial sectors are showing the highest demand for electric vehicles?",
              "a": "Currently, adoption demand is primarily led by public municipalities and state entities backed by legislative funding. Private transport interest remains limited unless supported by strong capital grant initiatives."
            },
            {
              "q": "Are your vehicle technicians certified to handle electric commercial truck repairs?",
              "a": "Yes. Our facility maintains factory-trained technicians backed by direct OEM technical support and specialized high-voltage diagnostic equipment to process battery balancing, electrical diagnostics, and motor maintenance safely."
            },
            {
              "q": "What electric truck platforms are currently available for order at your dealership?",
              "a": "Our supported electromobility lineup focuses on heavy-duty Class 8 operations, highlighting the BYD-8TT tandem-axle tractor and the BYD-8Y terminal yard tractor, alongside specialized Motiv-Workhorse all-electric bus and box truck options."
            }
          ]
        },
